# Retail Bank Transaction Analysis
## Power BI Project Documentation

### 1. Project Overview

The Retail Bank Transaction Analysis project focuses on analysing banking operations using Microsoft Power BI.

The project includes customer, account, branch, transaction, loan, loan payment, and card datasets. I used Power Query to clean and transform the data, created relationships between tables, and developed five interactive dashboard pages.

The main purpose is to understand customer behaviour, account activity, transaction trends, loan performance, and card usage through meaningful KPIs and visualisations.

### 2. Problem Statement

Banks maintain large amounts of data related to customers, accounts, transactions, loans, repayments, and cards. When this information is stored in separate datasets, it becomes difficult to understand overall banking performance and identify important business trends.

This project aims to combine and analyse these datasets using Power BI. Interactive dashboards and KPIs help users monitor banking activities, identify customer behaviour patterns, evaluate loan repayment performance, and understand product usage.

### 3. Project Objectives

- Analyse customer distribution across different segments.
- Understand account activity and branch performance.
- Identify transaction patterns and monthly trends.
- Monitor loan amounts and repayment behaviour.
- Analyse card activation and product engagement.
- Build interactive dashboards using KPIs, charts, and slicers.
- Generate business insights to support better decision-making.

